{"term":"equip","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3fcbde19ff031ed6c7","definition":"To supply with something necessary in order to carry out a specific action or task; to provide with (e.g. weapons, provisions, munitions, rigging).","example":"1698-1699, Edmund Ludlow, Memoirs\nGave orders for equipping a considerable fleet.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["apparel","dight","fit out","kit out"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bind on equip","equipable","equipper","overequip","re-equip","reequip","underequip","unequip"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equip#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fe3cbc39030e2e44c1","definition":"To dress up; to array; to clothe.","example":"The country are led astray in following the town, and equipped in a ridiculous habit, when they fancy themselves in the height of the mode.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["don"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bind on equip","equipable","equipper","overequip","re-equip","reequip","underequip","unequip"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equip#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7f3edf82ba0820ebc1","definition":"To prepare (someone) with a skill.","example":"I'm sorry, but I don't feel equipped to answer that kinda question yet.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["dress","put on"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["bind on equip","equipable","equipper","overequip","re-equip","reequip","underequip","unequip"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equip#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b76607aa09bb331cd8","definition":"To equip oneself with (an i